  "scope": "QEMU 11.1.2, TCG on Apple Silicon, q35, 256 MiB, 2 vCPUs, default x86 CPU, 1280x800 framebuffer",
  "workload": "Unchanged boot to first shell prompt, including 512 MiB allocation demo and timer sleep",
  "reason": "Reclaimed heap-tail clearing takes 70.5% of kernel startup and 22.9% of full boot on the measured setup.",
  "hypothesis": "Replacing REP STOSB with REP STOSQ for the already word-aligned heap tail reduces the repeated stores in TCG while zeroing exactly the same bytes. Expected local gain: about 8x. Amdahl projection at 8x: about 2.61x kernel startup and 1.25x full boot.",
  "proposal": "perf: take out the garbage eight bytes at a time",
